            <p>Understanding aerosol systems is fundamental to designing safe, stable, and commercially successful aerosol products. The choice of aerosol system directly affects product performance, regulatory compliance, filling feasibility, shelf life, and end-user experience.</p>
            <p>This article provides a fact-based technical explanation of the four primary aerosol systems used globally:</p>
            <ul style="display:block;list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;">
                <li>Solution</li>
                <li>Emulsion</li>
                <li>Suspension</li>
                <li>Bag-on-Valve (BOV)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>It is written for students, startup founders, product developers, and industrial entrepreneurs operating in India and international markets.</p>
            <figure style="max-width:720px;margin:0.5rem auto 0.75rem;">
                <img src="https://assets.zyrosite.com/A3QlOV94WLSaL6xE/overview-of-aerosol-system-types-diagram.jpg-uPf21xndDCAkvCqa.png"
