        <section class="section gradient-section" id="faq">
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Which aerosol system is the cheapest to manufacture?</h3>
                <p>Solution aerosol systems typically have the lowest manufacturing cost due to simple formulation and filling.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Which aerosol system is safest for pharmaceuticals?</h3>
                <p>Bag-on-Valve systems are preferred due to zero propellant–product contact and high sterility control.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Can one product use more than one aerosol system?</h3>
                <p>Yes. Some formulations can be adapted across systems with major formulation and valve redesign.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Why do suspension aerosols clog more frequently?</h3>
                <p>Due to solid particle settling, agglomeration, and mechanical wear of valve components.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is BOV mandatory for food aerosols?</h3>
                <p>While not always mandatory, it is highly preferred due to contamination control and regulatory acceptance.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

